Commercial S3.2 startup-probe diagnosis
=========================================

Observed at: 2026-08-29T15:36:40Z
Service: tu1nz-adult-commercial-s3.service
Probe: tu1nz-adult-commercial-s3-probe.service

Safe symptom
------------

The transient startup probe exited with status 2 before phase 01 evidence was
created. The main service remained inactive, Restart remained no, NRestarts
remained zero, and the disabled contract plus consumed S3.1 bootstrap
authorization were restored to their exact prior hashes.

Proven root cause
-----------------

systemd exposes LoadCredential material to the chatops service process as a
root-owned directory with mode 0550 and root-owned files with mode 0440. A
named ACL grants only chatops the required read/search access. The original
S3CredentialBoundary accepted only the local test representation 0700/0600,
so it rejected the real systemd representation before S3StartupRecorder was
constructed.

No credential contents were read into evidence or logs. Only path class,
ownership, modes, file sizes, ACL access class, process identity and a
one-byte non-empty read result were inspected.

Correction boundary
-------------------

The application accepts exactly two credential profiles:

1. current-user-owned local private credentials at 0700/0600;
2. root-owned systemd credentials directly under /run/credentials at
   0550/0440, provided the effective service identity can actually read them.

Symlinks, non-regular files, additional links, other paths, other owners,
broader modes, empty material and oversized material remain rejected.

Rollback
--------

Restore application commit 05fd8b44f533fa34c3baeeb0dd1db2ae2e679c0a
and its matching runtime verification authorization. This returns to the
pre-fix state but also restores the proven pre-phase-01 probe failure.
